# CLAUDE.md

Internal business application. Not public facing. Keep this file under 200 lines.

## Stack

- Frontend: React 19 + Vite + TypeScript (`strict: true`)
- Backend: Node.js 22 + Apollo Server + TypeScript
- API: GraphQL, SDL first, types generated with graphql-codegen
- Database: PostgreSQL + Sequelize 6
- Validation: Zod, shared between client and server
- Data fetching: Apollo Client
- UI: MUI Material 9 + `@mui/icons-material` + `@mui/x-data-grid`, styled with Emotion
- npm workspaces

## Commands

```bash
npm run dev                 # web + api in parallel
npm run typecheck           # tsc --noEmit, all packages
npm run lint                # eslint, zero warnings allowed
npm run lint:fix
npm test                    # vitest
npm run codegen             # regenerate GraphQL types, run after any .graphql change
npm run db:migrate
npm run db:migrate:undo
npm run db:seed

npm ci                      # install, never `npm install` in CI
npm run dev -w apps/web     # single workspace
```

Never edit `package-lock.json` by hand. Add a dependency with `npm install <pkg> -w apps/<app>` and commit the lockfile in the same change.

Gate before finishing any task, in this order: `npm run codegen` (if schema touched), `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint`, `npm test`. Do not report a task as done if any of them fails.

## Structure

```
apps/web/src/
  ├── features/<name>/
  │     ├── operations.graphql   queries and mutations for this feature
  │     ├── hooks.ts             wrappers around generated Apollo hooks
  │     ├── components/
  │     └── pages/
  ├── components/                shared presentational components, no business logic
  ├── theme/
  │     ├── index.ts             createTheme, palette, typography, shape
  │     ├── components.ts        MUI component overrides and defaultProps
  │     └── tokens.ts            colors, radii, spacing constants
  ├── generated/graphql.ts       generated, do not edit
  ├── i18n/                      locale files
  ├── lib/
  └── main.tsx

apps/api/src/
  ├── modules/<name>/
  │     ├── schema.graphql       SDL for this module
  │     ├── resolvers.ts         thin, no business logic
  │     ├── service.ts           business logic, no GraphQL context handling
  │     ├── model.ts             Sequelize model
  │     └── loaders.ts           DataLoader instances
  ├── db/
  │     ├── migrations/          generated, do not edit
  │     ├── seeders/
  │     └── index.ts
  ├── generated/graphql.ts       generated resolver types, do not edit
  ├── context.ts                 request context: user, loaders, transaction
  ├── env.ts                     validated environment variables
  └── server.ts
```

Feature names match between `apps/web/src/features/` and `apps/api/src/modules/`.

## Rules

1. Layers on the API: resolver reads args and context only, service holds logic, model holds persistence. A resolver never queries the database directly.
2. Every mutation input is validated with a Zod schema in the service before any write.
3. Types come from `generated/graphql.ts` or from Zod inference. Never declared twice by hand.
4. No `any`, no `@ts-ignore`, no non-null assertion `!` outside tests.
5. Environment variables only through `env.ts`.
6. No barrel files. Import concrete paths via the `@/` alias.
7. One exported component per file.
8. Errors: services throw a typed `AppError` with a machine readable `code`. The Apollo error formatter is the only place that maps it to a GraphQL error.
9. No raw SQL string interpolation. Use Sequelize finders or `replacements`.

## GraphQL conventions

- Every list field is paginated: `items`, `totalCount`, `hasNextPage`. No unbounded lists.
- Mutations take a single `input` argument and return a payload type, never a bare scalar.
- Nullability is deliberate. Non-null by default, nullable only when the domain allows absence.
- Every association resolver goes through a DataLoader. An association resolved with a direct query is a bug.
- Deprecate fields with `@deprecated(reason: "...")`, never delete them in the same change.
- After editing any `.graphql` file, run `npm run codegen` before typechecking.

## Sequelize conventions

- Models typed with `InferAttributes` / `InferCreationAttributes`. No untyped `Model`.
- Table names snake_case plural, columns snake_case, exposed to TypeScript as camelCase via `underscored: true`.
- Associations declared in one place, `apps/api/src/db/associations.ts`, not scattered across models.
- Schema changes go through a migration file. Never `sync({ alter: true })` outside tests.
- Multi-write operations run inside a transaction taken from the request context.
- Always scope reads by tenant or owner in the service, never rely on the resolver to do it.

## Material UI conventions

- Never hardcode a color, radius, spacing or font size. Read them from the theme: `theme.palette.primary.main`, `theme.spacing(2)`, `theme.shape.borderRadius`.
- A value that is not in the theme and is needed twice goes into `theme/tokens.ts` first.
- Recurring visual changes go into `theme/components.ts` as `styleOverrides` or `defaultProps`, not repeated `sx` props across files.
- `sx` is for one off layout adjustments only. More than about 8 keys means the component needs `styled()` or a theme override.
- No inline `style={{}}`, no CSS files per component, no `!important`.
- Layout with `Stack`, `Grid` and `Box`. No manual flexbox utility soup.
- Icons come from `@mui/icons-material`. No emoji anywhere in the UI, no icon fonts, no inline SVG for standard icons.
- Lists use `@mui/x-data-grid` with server side pagination wired to the GraphQL `items` / `totalCount` shape. Never load all rows and paginate client side.
- Column definitions live outside the component body, or in `useMemo`, never rebuilt on each render.
- Light mode only unless stated otherwise. Do not add a dark palette speculatively.
- Dialogs, menus and drawers use MUI components. No custom modal implementation.
- Feedback: `Snackbar` or the toast helper for transient messages, `Alert` for inline state, `Skeleton` for loading, never a bare spinner on a full page.

## Naming

- Files kebab-case, components PascalCase.
- Hooks: `useInvoices`, `useCreateInvoice`.
- GraphQL operations named after the feature: `query InvoiceList`, `mutation InvoiceCreate`.
- No `utils.ts` catch-all. Name the file after what it does.

## Size limits

| Type | Target | Hard max |
|---|---|---|
| React component | 80-150 | 250 |
| Page component | 60-120 | 200 |
| Resolvers file | 50-120 | 200 |
| Service | 100-200 | 300 |
| Sequelize model | 60-150 | 250 |
| SDL file | 50-150 | 250 |
| Hook | 40-80 | 150 |
| Utility | 20-60 | 100 |
| Test | - | 400 |

- Functions: 60 lines max, 4 parameters max, cyclomatic complexity 12 max.
- More than 5 exported functions in one file means it should be split.
- JSX blocks over 100 lines or nested deeper than 3 levels mean a component is missing.
- Exempt: `generated/`, `migrations/`, `seeders/`, config files, constant tables.

Enforced in `eslint.config.js` via `max-lines`, `max-lines-per-function`, `max-params`, `complexity`. Do not disable these rules inline to make code fit.

## Lint and typecheck

- ESLint runs with `--max-warnings=0`. A warning is a failure.
- `eslint-disable` requires a reason comment on the same line.
- `tsc --noEmit` must pass on every package before a task is done.
- Formatting is Prettier, never hand adjusted.

## Testing

- Vitest everywhere. Tests colocated: `service.test.ts` next to `service.ts`.
- Required: every service function, every non-trivial utility, every reducer.
- Not required: presentational components, generated code, thin resolvers.
- Integration tests hit a real Postgres test database inside a rolled back transaction. No mocking of Sequelize.
- One behaviour per test, named `it("rejects an invoice with a past due date")`.
- Fixtures live in `test/factories/`, never inline blobs copied between files.

## JSDoc

- Required on: exported service functions, custom hooks, permission checks, cache invalidation, anything with non-obvious business rules.
- Not required on: React components, types, obvious getters, tests.
- Document the why and the edge cases. Never restate the signature.

```ts
/**
 * Cancels an invoice and releases the reserved stock.
 * Throws if the invoice is already paid, cancellation is only allowed while status is DRAFT or SENT.
 */
```

## Documentation

- `README.md`: setup, environment variables, how to run.
- `docs/architecture.md`: request flow, module map, transaction and auth boundaries.
- `docs/decisions/NNNN-title.md`: one short ADR per structural decision, problem, choice, consequence.
- Update the doc in the same change as the code. A stale doc is worse than no doc.
- Every markdown file in `docs/` starts with the same YAML header as this file: `name`, `description`, `updated`.

## Mobile and responsive

- Layout must work down to the `md` breakpoint. Below that, only read views need to be usable.
- Breakpoints only through `theme.breakpoints`, never a raw media query string.
- DataGrid collapses into stacked `Card` items under `md`. No horizontal scrolling of the whole page.
- Touch targets at least 44px, enforced in `theme/components.ts` with a `@media (pointer: coarse)` override on `Button` and `IconButton`.
- Text inputs are 16px on touch to prevent iOS zoom.
- Dialogs use full width with 16px margins under `sm`.
- Not a mobile first product. Do not spend effort on phone specific layouts unless asked.

## PWA

- Installable with a manifest and an app icon, used for kiosk and tablet deployments.
- Service worker caches the app shell and static assets only. Never cache GraphQL responses.
- Offline state shows an explicit banner. No optimistic writes while offline.
- Version the service worker and force reload on activation to avoid stale bundles.

## Accessibility

- Use the MUI component that carries the right semantics. A `Box` with `onClick` is not acceptable, use `Button`, `IconButton` or `ListItemButton`.
- Every field uses `TextField` with a real `label`, or an explicit `InputLabel` linked by id. Every `IconButton` has an `aria-label`.
- Keep MUI focus rings. `Dialog` and `Drawer` already trap and restore focus, do not disable that.
- Tooltips are never the only carrier of information.
- Full keyboard operation for the main workflows: navigation, forms, tables, dialogs.
- Contrast ratio 4.5:1 minimum for text.
- `eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y` runs as an error, not a warning.

## Internationalisation

- All user facing strings go through the i18n layer. No literal text in JSX.
- Keys namespaced by feature: `invoices.form.dueDate.label`.
- Locales: `fr` default, `en`, `nl`. Adding a key means adding it to all three files.
- Dates, numbers and currency formatted with `Intl`, never manually.
- Server side messages return an error `code` plus params. The client does the translation.

## Not applicable

SEO, sitemaps, meta tags, structured data, server side rendering for crawlers. The application sits behind authentication. Do not add them.

## Do not touch

- `apps/api/src/db/migrations/` and `seeders/`
- `generated/` in either app, regenerate with `npm run codegen`
- `dist/`, `node_modules/`, lockfiles

